<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sybaris</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sybaris was a Greek city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-taranto">Gulf of Taranto</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, founded by Achaean colonists around 720 BCE and so wealthy that its name became a byword for luxury. It was destroyed by its rival Croton in 510 BCE. Descendants of its citizens took part in the Panhellenic foundation of Thurii nearby in 444/443 BCE but were soon expelled after quarrels with the other settlers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sybaris.jpg" alt="Sybaris" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mboesch · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sibari-scavi-teatro.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
